.TH "KEYORIX" "1" "" "Keyorix CLI" "Keyorix Manual"
.SH NAME
keyorix \- Command\-line client for the Keyorix secrets manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keyorix
[\fIglobal flags\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIflags\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
keyorix is the Keyorix CLI. It talks to a Keyorix server exclusively over the REST API; it has no local database mode. Host\-side operations (config/keys/database setup, encryption key rotation) are "keyorix\-server admin", a separate command.
.PP
Exit codes:
.nf
  0  success
  1  the request was refused or failed (conflict, validation error, server error); "doctor": a check failed
  2  usage error: unknown command, bad or missing flag or argument
  3  not logged in, or the session was rejected (HTTP 401): run "keyorix login"
  4  permission denied (HTTP 403)
  5  not found (HTTP 404)
  6  the server could not be reached (network, TLS certificate refused, redirect)
.fi
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-file\fR \fIstring\fR
PEM CA/certificate file to trust for the server's TLS certificate, instead of the system roots (or set KEYORIX_CA_FILE, or: keyorix config set ca_file <path>)
.SH COMMANDS
.SS keyorix access\-review
Review who has role\-based access to a project's secrets (ISO 27001 A.5.18)
.PP
List every principal (user or group) that can reach a project's secrets via an assigned role, with the highest secrets action that role grants \(em the role\-based standing\-access surface for periodic access recertification. Requires roles.read at the project scope.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix access\-review [command] [flags]\fR
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Project to review (required)
.SS keyorix access\-review attest
Attest an access\-review grant (certify it was reviewed and kept)
.PP
Record that the grant identified by the flags was reviewed and intentionally kept \(em the audit evidence of recertification (access_review.attested). Changes no access. Requires roles.read at the project scope.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix access\-review attest [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
# Attest that a role grant is still needed
keyorix access\-review attest \-\-project\-id 3 \-\-source role \-\-role\-id 4 \-\-principal\-id 12
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-environment\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Environment scope of a role grant (0 = whole project)
.TP
\fB\-\-principal\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
User or group ID the grant is for (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-principal\-type\fR \fIstring\fR
Principal type: user|group (for role grants) (default user)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Project the grant belongs to (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-role\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Role ID (required when \-\-source=role)
.TP
\fB\-\-secret\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Secret ID (required when \-\-source=direct_share|group_share)
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fIstring\fR
Grant source: role|direct_share|group_share (required)
.SS keyorix access\-review campaign
Manage access\-review campaigns (periodic recertification cycles, A.5.18)
.PP
Run periodic access recertification as a tracked campaign: open snapshots the project's current access into reviewable items, decide attests or revokes each, and close freezes the cycle as audit evidence.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix access\-review campaign [command]\fR
.SS keyorix access\-review campaign close
Close a campaign (freeze as evidence); refuses pending items unless \-\-force
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix access\-review campaign close [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix access\-review campaign close \-\-project\-id 3 \-\-campaign\-id 7
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-campaign\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Campaign to close (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Close even if items remain pending
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Project (required)
.SS keyorix access\-review campaign decide
Decide on one campaign item: attest (keep) or revoke
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix access\-review campaign decide [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix access\-review campaign decide \-\-project\-id 3 \-\-campaign\-id 7 \-\-item\-id 41 \-\-action attest
keyorix access\-review campaign decide \-\-project\-id 3 \-\-campaign\-id 7 \-\-item\-id 42 \-\-action revoke \-\-reason "left the team"
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-action\fR \fIstring\fR
attest | revoke (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-campaign\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Campaign (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-item\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Item to decide (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Project (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIstring\fR
Optional reviewer note
.SS keyorix access\-review campaign list
List a project's access\-review campaigns
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix access\-review campaign list [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix access\-review campaign list \-\-project\-id 3
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIstring\fR
Output format: table, json or yaml (default table)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Project (required)
.SS keyorix access\-review campaign open
Open a new access\-review campaign (snapshots current access)
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix access\-review campaign open [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix access\-review campaign open \-\-project\-id 3 \-\-name "Q4 2026 access recertification"
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fIstring\fR
Campaign name (e.g. "Q4 2026 access recertification")
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Project to review (required)
.SS keyorix access\-review campaign show
Show a campaign and its items (snapshot + decisions)
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix access\-review campaign show [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix access\-review campaign show \-\-project\-id 3 \-\-campaign\-id 7
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-campaign\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Campaign to show (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Project (required)
.SS keyorix access\-review revoke
Revoke an access\-review grant (remove the role assignment or share)
.PP
Remove the grant identified by the flags \(em a project\-scoped role assignment (\-\-source role \-\-role\-id N) or a secret share (\-\-source direct_share|group_share \-\-secret\-id N). The removal is audited (access_review.revoked). Requires roles.assign at the project scope.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix access\-review revoke [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
# Revoke a user's role grant found during a review
keyorix access\-review revoke \-\-project\-id 3 \-\-source role \-\-role\-id 4 \-\-principal\-id 12
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-environment\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Environment scope of a role grant (0 = whole project)
.TP
\fB\-\-principal\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
User or group ID the grant is for (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-principal\-type\fR \fIstring\fR
Principal type: user|group (for role grants) (default user)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Project the grant belongs to (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-role\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Role ID (required when \-\-source=role)
.TP
\fB\-\-secret\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Secret ID (required when \-\-source=direct_share|group_share)
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fIstring\fR
Grant source: role|direct_share|group_share (required)
.SS keyorix anomalies
Manage anomaly detection alerts
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix anomalies [command]\fR
.SS keyorix anomalies acknowledge
Acknowledge an anomaly alert
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix anomalies acknowledge <id>\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix anomalies acknowledge 17
.fi
.SS keyorix anomalies config
Manage anomaly detection runtime configuration
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix anomalies config [command]\fR
.SS keyorix anomalies config get
Show the current anomaly detection configuration
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix anomalies config get\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix anomalies config get
.fi
.SS keyorix anomalies config set
Update one or more anomaly detection configuration fields
.PP
Update the anomaly detection runtime configuration.
.PP
Only flags that are explicitly provided are changed; all others keep their current stored values. Changes take effect on the next detection scan without restarting the server.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix anomalies config set [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
# Treat 22:00\-06:00 New York time as off\-hours
keyorix anomalies config set \-\-off\-hours\-enabled \-\-off\-hours\-start 22 \-\-off\-hours\-end 6 \-\-off\-hours\-timezone America/New_York
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-lookback\-days\fR \fIint\fR
Lookback window for baseline (days)
.TP
\fB\-\-ml\-enabled\fR
Enable ML (Isolation Forest) anomaly detection
.TP
\fB\-\-ml\-num\-trees\fR \fIint\fR
ML Isolation Forest tree count
.TP
\fB\-\-ml\-sample\-size\fR \fIint\fR
ML Isolation Forest per\-tree subsample size
.TP
\fB\-\-ml\-threshold\fR \fIfloat64\fR
ML anomaly\-score threshold (0.5\(en1.0)
.TP
\fB\-\-off\-hours\-enabled\fR
Enable off\-hours rule
.TP
\fB\-\-off\-hours\-end\fR \fIint\fR
Off\-hours band end hour (0\(en23)
.TP
\fB\-\-off\-hours\-start\fR \fIint\fR
Off\-hours band start hour (0\(en23)
.TP
\fB\-\-off\-hours\-timezone\fR \fIstring\fR
IANA timezone for off\-hours band (e.g. America/New_York)
.TP
\fB\-\-quarantine\-hours\fR \fIint\fR
Quarantine period before a new actor is trusted (hours)
.SS keyorix anomalies escalation
Manage alert escalation policies
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix anomalies escalation [command]\fR
.SS keyorix anomalies escalation create
Create an alert escalation policy
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix anomalies escalation create [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix anomalies escalation create \-\-name page\-oncall \-\-min\-severity high \-\-after\-minutes 15 \-\-channels 1,2
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-after\-minutes\fR \fIint\fR
Escalate if unacknowledged for this many minutes (default 30)
.TP
\fB\-\-channels\fR \fIstring\fR
Comma\-separated NotificationChannel IDs
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-severity\fR \fIstring\fR
Minimum severity to escalate: low|medium|high|critical (default medium)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fIstring\fR
Policy name (required)
.SS keyorix anomalies escalation delete
Delete an alert escalation policy
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix anomalies escalation delete <id>\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix anomalies escalation delete 3
.fi
.SS keyorix anomalies escalation list
List alert escalation policies
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix anomalies escalation list [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix anomalies escalation list
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIstring\fR
Output format: table, json or yaml (default table)
.SS keyorix anomalies escalation run
Trigger the alert escalation job immediately
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix anomalies escalation run\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix anomalies escalation run
.fi
.SS keyorix anomalies list
List anomaly alerts
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix anomalies list [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix anomalies list \-\-unacknowledged
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIstring\fR
Output format: table, json or yaml (default table)
.TP
\fB\-\-unacknowledged\fR
Show only unacknowledged alerts
.SS keyorix audit
Verify and export the tamper\-evident audit trail
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix audit [command]\fR
.SS keyorix audit checkpoint
Write a signed checkpoint of the current audit\-chain head (ADR\-029)
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix audit checkpoint\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix audit checkpoint
.fi
.SS keyorix audit export
Stream the audit feed as NDJSON (one event per line) for SIEM pull
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix audit export [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
# Export the whole audit trail as NDJSON
keyorix audit export \-\-all > audit.ndjson
# ...or as CSV, from a point in time
keyorix audit export \-\-all \-\-csv \-\-since 2026\-10\-01T00:00:00Z > audit.csv
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-after\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Resume after this event id (exclusive cursor)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Follow the cursor to the end, emitting every event
.TP
\fB\-\-csv\fR
Emit CSV (header + one row per event) instead of NDJSON
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIint\fR
Events per page (1\(en1000) (default 100)
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fIstring\fR
Only export events at/after this time (RFC3339)
.SS keyorix audit logs
Query the audit trail with filters (human\-readable table)
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix audit logs [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix audit logs \-\-limit 20
keyorix audit logs \-\-project\-id 3 \-\-event\-type secret.read \-\-since 2026\-10\-01T00:00:00Z
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-actor\-type\fR \fIstring\fR
Filter by actor kind: user | machine_identity | system
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fIstring\fR
Continue after a previous page (the cursor printed under it)
.TP
\fB\-\-event\-type\fR \fIstring\fR
Filter by event type (e.g. secret.read, secret.deleted)
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-total\fR
Count every matching event (exact total; slower on a large audit trail)
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIint\fR
Max events to show (1\(en100) (default 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Filter by project id
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fIstring\fR
Only events at/after this time (RFC3339)
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fIstring\fR
Only events at/before this time (RFC3339)
.TP
\fB\-\-user\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Filter by actor user id
.SS keyorix audit migrate\-chain\-encoding
One\-time re\-derivation of the audit hash chain under the current encoding
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix audit migrate\-chain\-encoding [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
# Preview first; nothing is written without \-\-confirm
keyorix audit migrate\-chain\-encoding
keyorix audit migrate\-chain\-encoding \-\-confirm
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-confirm\fR
Apply the migration for real. Without this flag, the command only previews what would change \(em nothing is written.
.SS keyorix audit search
Search the audit trail with structured filters
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix audit search [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix audit search \-\-action secret.read \-\-actor alice \-\-success false
keyorix audit search \-\-resource\-type secret \-\-resource\-id 42
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-action\fR \fIstring\fR
Filter by exact event type (e.g. secret.read)
.TP
\fB\-\-actor\fR \fIstring\fR
Partial match on actor username
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fIstring\fR
Continue after a previous page (the cursor printed under it)
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-total\fR
Count every matching event (exact total; slower on a large audit trail)
.TP
\fB\-\-ip\fR \fIstring\fR
Filter by originating IP address
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIint\fR
Max results (1\(en1000) (default 100)
.TP
\fB\-\-offset\fR \fIint\fR
Pagination offset (offset+limit up to 10000; use \-\-cursor beyond)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Filter by project ID
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Filter by exact resource ID (secret_node_id)
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\-type\fR \fIstring\fR
Filter by resource kind (e.g. secret, user, role)
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fIstring\fR
Only events at/after this RFC3339 time
.TP
\fB\-\-success\fR \fIstring\fR
Filter by outcome: true or false
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fIstring\fR
Only events at/before this RFC3339 time
.TP
\fB\-\-user\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Filter by exact actor user ID
.SS keyorix audit verify
Report the audit hash chain's integrity (non\-zero exit if broken or not proven)
.PP
Report the audit hash chain's integrity.
.PP
By default this reads the server's incremental verification: the rolling full re\-walk (every row re\-hashed at least once per cycle) plus a check of the rows after the latest signed checkpoint. Status is VALID, BROKEN, or NOT PROVEN (no recent full verification covers the older rows yet). \-\-full runs a full walk on the server now, as a background job, and waits for it.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix audit verify [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
# Check the audit hash chain
keyorix audit verify
# Walk the whole chain on the server and print the result as JSON
keyorix audit verify \-\-full \-\-json
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-full\fR
Run a full walk of the chain on the server now (a background job) and wait for its result
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the raw verification result as JSON (for recording the external anchor)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIduration\fR
With \-\-full: how long to wait for the job (default 30m0s)
.SS keyorix billing
FinOps billing and usage reports (requires billing license feature)
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix billing [command]\fR
.SS keyorix billing report
Generate a per\-project billing report for a date range
.PP
Generate a per\-project billing report showing secret counts, reads, writes, rotations, unique human users, and machine reads for the specified date window (GET /admin/billing/report). Requires audit.read and the "billing" license feature.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix billing report [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix billing report \-\-from 2026\-09\-01T00:00:00Z \-\-to 2026\-10\-01T00:00:00Z
keyorix billing report \-\-from 2026\-09\-01T00:00:00Z \-\-to 2026\-10\-01T00:00:00Z \-\-project\-id 3,5 \-o json
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fIstring\fR
Start of billing window, RFC3339 (e.g. 2026\-01\-01T00:00:00Z) \(em required
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIstring\fR
Output format: table, json or yaml (default table)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIstring\fR
Comma\-separated project IDs to include (omit for all)
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fIstring\fR
End of billing window, RFC3339 (e.g. 2026\-02\-01T00:00:00Z) \(em required
.SS keyorix break\-glass
Self\-service emergency access (incident response)
.PP
Activate emergency access to a project: immediately self\-grant the configured emergency role, time\-bound and auto\-expiring, with a written justification. Every activation is loudly audited and alerts the project's admins. Use list/revoke to review and end activations.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix break\-glass [command]\fR
.SS keyorix break\-glass activate
Activate emergency access (self\-grant the emergency role, time\-bound)
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix break\-glass activate [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix break\-glass activate \-\-project\-id 3 \-\-justification "prod outage INC\-1234" \-\-ttl 2h
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-justification\fR \fIstring\fR
Written reason for emergency access (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIuint32\fR
Project to activate emergency access for (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fIstring\fR
Grant lifetime override, e.g. 2h (default + capped by server config)
.SS keyorix break\-glass list
List a project's break\-glass activations (all with roles.read, else your own as a member)
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix break\-glass list [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix break\-glass list \-\-project\-id 3
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIuint32\fR
Project (required)
.SS keyorix break\-glass revoke
Revoke an active emergency grant early
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix break\-glass revoke [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix break\-glass revoke \-\-project\-id 3 \-\-activation\-id 9
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-activation\-id\fR \fIuint32\fR
Activation to revoke (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIuint32\fR
Project (required)
.SS keyorix bundle
Air\-gap update bundles: verify and import offline
.PP
Verify and stage Keyorix air\-gap update bundles (ADR\-062 Phase 1).
.PP
A bundle is a single signed tarball carrying a release's artifacts, pinned by sha256 in a manifest that is signed with an offline ed25519 key. An air\-gapped operator carries the file across the gap and verifies it offline against the public key embedded in this binary at build time \-\- trust follows a pinned chain, never a key shipped inside the bundle. "bundle build" (signing a new release) is maintainer\-only tooling and lives in the old CLI.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix bundle [command]\fR
.SS keyorix bundle import
Verify a bundle offline and stage its artifacts into a directory
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix bundle import <bundle> [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix bundle import update\-1.4.0.bundle \-\-dest /var/lib/keyorix/updates \-\-installed\-version 1.3.2 \-\-license /etc/keyorix/license.token
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-deployment\-id\fR \fIstring\fR
this deployment's configured license.deployment_id, if the license is deployment\-bound
.TP
\fB\-\-dest\fR \fIstring\fR
directory to stage verified artifacts into (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
proceed without \-\-installed\-version on a first import into \-\-dest (dangerous \-\- skips the no\-downgrade / anti\-skip check)
.TP
\fB\-\-installed\-version\fR \fIstring\fR
currently\-installed version, to enforce no\-downgrade / min\-upgrade\-from (required on a first import into \-\-dest, unless \-\-force)
.TP
\fB\-\-license\fR \fIstring\fR
path to the installed license token (bundle import is a commercial feature)
.TP
\fB\-\-reset\-install\-state\fR
acknowledge that \-\-dest's install state was intentionally reset (e.g. \-\-dest was deliberately cleared or recreated): required when the external install\-state record disagrees with \-\-dest itself, otherwise refused as a possible downgrade\-reset attempt
.SS keyorix bundle verify
Verify a bundle offline against the embedded pinned key and component digests
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix bundle verify <bundle> [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix bundle verify update\-1.4.0.bundle \-\-installed\-version 1.3.2
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
proceed without \-\-installed\-version (dangerous \-\- skips the no\-downgrade / anti\-skip check, verifies signature and digests only)
.TP
\fB\-\-installed\-version\fR \fIstring\fR
currently\-installed version, to enforce no\-downgrade / min\-upgrade\-from (required unless \-\-force)
.SS keyorix change\-password
Change your own password (drops your other sessions)
.PP
change\-password calls POST /auth/change\-password to set a new password for the currently logged\-in account. Every other active session belonging to this account is revoked as a result \-\- the current one is not.
.PP
This is the command to run right after logging in with a one\-time password (e.g. the one keyorix\-server admin recover\-admin prints) \-\- the account stays confined to this command (and a handful of others) until a real password is set. With security.require_mfa on and no second factor yet, that login is a short setup session that must also enrol MFA ("keyorix mfa enroll" + "keyorix mfa activate", before or after this command); once both are done the session ends and the next "keyorix login" asks for a code.
.PP
Both passwords are read from a hidden prompt. In a script, set KEYORIX_CURRENT_PASSWORD and KEYORIX_NEW_PASSWORD (or KEYORIX_CURRENT_PASSWORD_FILE / KEYORIX_NEW_PASSWORD_FILE); passwords are never accepted as flags, because argv is visible to other users.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix change\-password\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
