Restrict the token to source IPs in this CIDR (repeatable; e.g. \-\-allowed\-cidr 10.0.0.0/8). Omit = no network restriction
.TP
\fB\-\-environment\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Confine the token to a single environment (0 = any; only with \-\-project\-id)
.TP
\fB\-\-expires\fR \fIstring\fR
Expiry (RFC3339 or YYYY\-MM\-DD; omit = never)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fIstring\fR
Token name (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Confine the token to a single project (0 = any)
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fIstringArray\fR
Least\-privilege permission (repeatable; e.g. \-\-scope secrets.read). Omit = inherit all your permissions
.SS keyorix pat hygiene
List stale or expired\-but\-active tokens across all users (admin)
.PP
Show the deployment\-wide personal access tokens that should probably be revoked: ones that have expired but were never revoked, and ones unused for a long window (token sprawl). Requires global audit.read. Never prints a token's secret.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix pat hygiene [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix pat hygiene \-\-days 60
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-days\fR \fIint\fR
Staleness window in days (default server\-side: 90, cap 3650)
