.nf
keyorix project env delete 9 \-\-project payments \-\-confirm
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-confirm\fR
Confirm deletion without interactive prompt
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fIstring\fR
Override the active project
.SS keyorix project env list
List environments for the active (or specified) project
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix project env list [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix project env list \-\-project payments
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIstring\fR
Output format: table, json or yaml (default table)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fIstring\fR
Override the active project
.SS keyorix project environments
List environments for a project
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix project environments <project\-id>\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix project environments 3
.fi
.SS keyorix project health
Show the secret health summary for a project
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix project health <name> [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix project health payments \-\-limit 10
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIint\fR
Maximum number of secrets to display (1\-100) (default 20)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIstring\fR
Output format: table, json or yaml (default table)
.SS keyorix project hygiene
Show a project's security\-hygiene posture (counts)
.PP
Summarize a project's outstanding cleanup signals in one call: secrets whose owner departed, secrets unused for a long window, secrets expiring/expired, and stale machine identities. Requires secrets.read at the project scope.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix project hygiene <project\-id>\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix project hygiene 3
.fi
.SS keyorix project list
List all projects
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix project list [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix project list
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIstring\fR
Output format: table, json or yaml (default table)
.SS keyorix project resume\-secrets
Resume every suspended secret in a project \-\- restore value reads
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix project resume\-secrets [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix project resume\-secrets \-\-id 3
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Project ID (required)
.SS keyorix project stats
Show rich statistics for a project
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix project stats <name> [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix project stats payments \-o json
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIstring\fR
Output format: table, json or yaml (default table)
.SS keyorix project suspend\-secrets
Suspend every secret in a project \-\- block value reads project\-wide
.PP
Freeze a whole project (a breach response): value reads of every active secret in the project that you may write are refused until you resume them. Versions, shares and the audit trail are preserved. Requires secrets.write on the project, the same as suspending one secret.
.PP
With \-\-clear\-synced\-copies the copies of those secrets synced to Kubernetes clusters (by the operator or keyorix\-k8s\-sync) are also emptied for the duration of THIS suspension, whatever each resource's own onSuspend setting says. Use it when the secrets are compromised, and rotate them afterwards. Resuming removes the request and the next sync restores the copies. Running suspend\-secrets again with the flag adds the request to secrets that are already suspended without it.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix project suspend\-secrets [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix project suspend\-secrets \-\-id 3 \-\-reason "suspected CI compromise"
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-synced\-copies\fR
Also clear the copies synced to Kubernetes clusters for this suspension (compromise response; rotate the secrets afterwards)
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Project ID (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIstring\fR
Optional reason recorded in the audit events
.SS keyorix project use
Set the active project for subsequent commands
.PP
Saves the active project name to the credentials file (cli/internal/credstore). All project\-scoped commands inherit this context; override per\-command with \-\-project.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix project use <name>\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
# Make "payments" the default for later commands
keyorix project use payments
.fi
.SS keyorix rbac
Role\-Based Access Control management commands
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix rbac [command]\fR
.SS keyorix rbac assign\-role
Assign a role to a user
.PP
Assign a role to a user by email address.
.PP
With \-\-project, the grant is scoped to that project only (rather than globally). With \-\-environment, the grant is further narrowed to a single environment within that project (\-\-project must also be supplied).
.PP
With \-\-ttl, the grant is time\-bound (just\-in\-time access): it stops authorizing once the window passes and is swept automatically. Useful for emergency or contractor access. Example: \-\-ttl 4h grants the role for four hours.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix rbac assign\-role [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix rbac assign\-role \-\-user alice@example.com \-\-role developer \-\-project payments
# Time\-bound grant
keyorix rbac assign\-role \-\-user alice@example.com \-\-role admin \-\-project payments \-\-ttl 4h
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-environment\fR \fIstring\fR
Scope the grant to this environment within \-\-project (optional; requires \-\-project)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fIstring\fR
Scope the grant to this project (optional)
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIstring\fR
Role name to assign (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fIduration\fR
Time\-bound grant lifetime (e.g. 4h, 30m); omit for a permanent grant
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fIstring\fR
User email address (required)
.SS keyorix rbac assign\-role\-to\-group
Assign a role to a group
.PP
Assign a role to a group.
.PP
With \-\-project, the grant is scoped to that project only. With \-\-environment, the grant is further narrowed to a single environment within that project (\-\-project must also be supplied).
.PP
With \-\-ttl, the grant is time\-bound (just\-in\-time access).
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix rbac assign\-role\-to\-group [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix rbac assign\-role\-to\-group \-\-group platform\-team \-\-role developer \-\-project payments
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-environment\fR \fIstring\fR
Scope the grant to this environment within \-\-project (optional; requires \-\-project)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fIstring\fR
Group name or numeric ID (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fIstring\fR
Scope the grant to this project (optional)
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIstring\fR
Role name to assign (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fIduration\fR
Time\-bound grant lifetime (e.g. 4h, 30m); omit for a permanent grant
.SS keyorix rbac audit\-logs
View RBAC audit logs
.PP
View audit logs for RBAC operations (role assignments, removals, permission grants).
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix rbac audit\-logs [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix rbac audit\-logs \-\-limit 20
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIint\fR
Maximum number of logs to retrieve (default 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-offset\fR \fIint\fR
Number of logs to skip
.SS keyorix rbac check\-permission
Check if a user has a specific permission
.PP
Check if a user has a specific permission by email address and permission name
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix rbac check\-permission [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix rbac check\-permission \-\-user alice@example.com \-\-permission secrets.read
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-permission\fR \fIstring\fR
Permission name to check (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fIstring\fR
User email address (required)
.SS keyorix rbac export\-matrix
Export the deployment\-wide RBAC permission matrix
.PP
Export every (user, role, permission, scope) tuple in the deployment.
.PP
Used by auditors for SOC2/ISO27001 access reviews. Output includes who holds what role/permission in what scope (global, project, or environment).
.PP
Supports table (default), JSON, and CSV output formats.
.PP
Examples:
.nf
  keyorix rbac export\-matrix
  keyorix rbac export\-matrix \-\-format csv \-\-output access\-review.csv
  keyorix rbac export\-matrix \-\-format json \-\-project production
.fi
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix rbac export\-matrix [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix rbac export\-matrix \-\-format csv \-\-output rbac\-matrix.csv
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIstring\fR
Output format: table, csv, or json (default table)
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fIstring\fR
Write output to this file (default: stdout)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fIstring\fR
Filter by project name (optional)
.SS keyorix rbac list\-group\-roles
List roles assigned to a group
.PP
List all roles assigned to a specific group.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix rbac list\-group\-roles [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
