keyorix sod violations
.fi
.SS keyorix status
Show the configured server, login state, and version\-skew check
.PP
status is the remote\-only successor to the old CLI's "status" command (docs/cli\-split\-inventory.md §2.7): it has no local/embedded branch to fall back to (ADR\-108 Decision A removes local mode entirely). Unlike the old command, it actually parses GET /health's response body instead of discarding it, and reports the GET /api/v1/version skew check.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix status\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
# Shows the server, who you are logged in as, and version compatibility
keyorix status
.fi
.SS keyorix system
Server info and on\-demand admin job triggers
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix system [command]\fR
.SS keyorix system info
Show the connected server's build identity and configuration
.PP
Display the remote Keyorix server's version, commit, runtime, and feature/security configuration (GET /system/info). Useful for confirming which build you're talking to. Requires a connection to a server and system.read.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix system info\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix system info
.fi
.SS keyorix system init
Bootstrap a running Keyorix server (admin user + default workspace)
.PP
Bootstrap a running Keyorix server: creates the admin user, default RBAC roles, and default workspace (project + 3 environments) via POST /system/init. Safe to run more than once \-\- idempotent.
.PP
This is the network\-bootstrap half only. Local host setup (config file, encryption keys, database) is "keyorix\-server admin init", a separate host\-filesystem tool this network\-only CLI does not run.
.PP
The admin password is read from KEYORIX_ADMIN_PASSWORD, or prompted for (hidden) when that is unset. The bootstrap token is read from KEYORIX_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN. Do not pass either on the command line: arguments are visible via ps/proc and saved in shell history.
.PP
Examples:
.nf
  keyorix system init \-\-server http://localhost:8080
  keyorix system init \-\-server https://vault.example.com \\
      \-\-admin\-username admin \-\-admin\-email admin@example.com
.fi
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix system init [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
# First\-run bootstrap of a new server; prompts for the admin password
keyorix system init \-\-server https://keyorix.example.com \-\-admin\-username admin \-\-admin\-email admin@example.com
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\-email\fR \fIstring\fR
Admin email address (default admin@localhost)
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\-username\fR \fIstring\fR
Admin username to create (default admin)
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fIstring\fR
Server base URL to bootstrap (required)
.SS keyorix system role\-expiry\-check
Trigger a role\-expiry notification scan on the connected server
.PP
Send immediate role\-expiry notifications for time\-bound role grants approaching their deadline (POST /api/v1/admin/jobs/role\-expiry\-check).
.PP
Warning notifications are sent for grants expiring within 7 days; critical notifications for those expiring within 1 day. Requires system.write.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix system role\-expiry\-check\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix system role\-expiry\-check
.fi
.SS keyorix system token\-expiry\-check
Trigger a PAT and machine\-credential expiry notification scan on the connected server
.PP
Send immediate expiry notifications for PersonalAccessTokens and MachineIdentityCredentials approaching their deadline (POST /api/v1/admin/jobs/token\-expiry\-check).
.PP
Warning notifications are sent for tokens expiring within 7 days; critical notifications for those expiring within 1 day. Requires system.write.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix system token\-expiry\-check\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix system token\-expiry\-check
.fi
.SS keyorix trust
Air\-gap signing\-key tooling (ed25519 keypairs for update bundles / licenses)
.PP
Generate and inspect the asymmetric keys Keyorix uses to sign air\-gapped update bundles and offline licenses (ADR\-062). The private key never ships; its public key is embedded into release builds so an air\-gapped deployment can verify offline.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix trust [command]\fR
.SS keyorix trust keygen
Generate an ed25519 signing keypair (update or license)
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix trust keygen [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix trust keygen \-\-purpose update \-\-key\-id update\-2026 \-\-dir ./keys
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-dir\fR \fIstring\fR
directory to write the keypair into (default \&.)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
overwrite an existing keypair at the target paths (dangerous)
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-id\fR \fIstring\fR
key identifier, e.g. update\-2026 (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-purpose\fR \fIstring\fR
key purpose: update | license (required)
.SS keyorix usage
View usage and activity reports
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix usage [command]\fR
.SS keyorix usage show
Show per\-project secret usage for a time window
.PP
Display a per\-project secret usage report (secret counts and read activity) for the given reporting window (GET /admin/usage). Requires audit.read.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix usage show [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix usage show \-\-days 30
keyorix usage show \-\-project\-id 3 \-o json
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-days\fR \fIint\fR
Reporting window in days (1\-365) (default 30)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIstring\fR
Output format: table, json or yaml (default table)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIint\fR
Scope to a single project (0 = all)
.SS keyorix user
Manage users
.PP
Create, read, update, delete, list, and manage the account lifecycle of users.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user [command]\fR
.SS keyorix user create
Create a new user
.PP
Create a new user. Supply \-\-password to set an initial password, or use \-\-setup\-link to provision an ADR\-028 setup link instead: the account is created in pending_first_login state and the user sets their own password via the link. In out\-of\-band mode the link is printed for you to relay.
.PP
Or use \-\-one\-time\-password to have the server generate an initial password (ADR\-028 Part E): the account is created in password_reset_required state, the password is printed once for you to relay, and the user must change it on first login.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user create [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
# Prompts for an initial password (or use \-\-setup\-link / \-\-one\-time\-password)
keyorix user create \-\-username bob \-\-email bob@example.com \-\-setup\-link
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIstring\fR
Acting admin email (unused in this REST\-only CLI \-\- kept for flag compatibility; the session behind your bearer token is always the acting admin)
.TP
\fB\-\-display\-name\fR \fIstring\fR
Display name (defaults to username)
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fIstring\fR
Email (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-one\-time\-password\fR
Generate a one\-time password instead of an admin\-set password (ADR\-028 Part E); must be changed on first login
.TP
\fB\-\-setup\-link\fR
Provision a setup link instead of an admin\-set password (ADR\-028)
.TP
\fB\-\-username\fR \fIstring\fR
Username (required)
.SS keyorix user delete
Delete a user
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user delete [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix user delete \-\-id 12
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIstring\fR
Acting admin email (required; unused in this REST\-only CLI \-\- kept for flag compatibility)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
User ID (required)
.SS keyorix user force\-password\-reset
Require a user to change their password at next login
.PP
Force a user into a restricted session until they change their password. They can authenticate but every endpoint except change\-password is blocked until then.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user force\-password\-reset [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix user force\-password\-reset \-\-id 12
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIstring\fR
Acting admin email (required; unused in this REST\-only CLI \-\- kept for flag compatibility)
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Target user ID (required)
.SS keyorix user get
Get a user by id or email
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user get [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix user get \-\-email bob@example.com
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fIstring\fR
User email
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
User ID
.SS keyorix user list
List users
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user list [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix user list \-\-page 1 \-\-page\-size 50
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIstring\fR
Output format: table, json or yaml (default table)
.TP
\fB\-\-page\fR \fIint\fR
Page number (default 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-page\-size\fR \fIint\fR
Page size (max 100) (default 20)
.SS keyorix user reactivate
Reactivate a user (restores login)
.PP
Return a suspended (or otherwise non\-active) user to the active state.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user reactivate [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix user reactivate \-\-id 12
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIstring\fR
Acting admin email (required; unused in this REST\-only CLI \-\- kept for flag compatibility)
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Target user ID (required)
.SS keyorix user reissue\-one\-time\-password
Issue a new one\-time password for an existing user
.PP
Issue a new server\-generated one\-time password for an existing user, for when the first one expired (see user create \-\-one\-time\-password) or was lost. <user> is a numeric user ID or an email address.
.PP
The password is printed once for you to relay out of band; it is never shown again. It expires after security.one_time_password_ttl (default 72h). The account is restricted to changing its password at the next login (and to MFA enrolment where the deployment requires MFA), and all of the user's existing sessions end. Needs the same permission as creating a user (users.write).
.PP
Refused for your own account (use `keyorix\-server admin recover\-admin`), for users managed by an external identity provider (SSO), and for suspended users.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user reissue\-one\-time\-password <user>\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix user reissue\-one\-time\-password bob
.fi
.SS keyorix user resend\-setup\-link
Reissue and redeliver a user's setup link (ADR\-028)
.PP
Reissue an account's setup link, invalidating any prior link, and deliver it again. In out\-of\-band mode the link is printed for you to relay. Throttled per the ADR\-028 resend limits.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user resend\-setup\-link [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix user resend\-setup\-link \-\-id 12
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIstring\fR
Acting admin email (required; unused in this REST\-only CLI \-\- kept for flag compatibility)
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Target user ID (required)
.SS keyorix user revoke\-sessions
Force\-logout a user (revoke all active sessions)
.PP
Terminate every active session of a user immediately, without changing their account state \(em for suspected session/token theft. The user can log back in after re\-authenticating. To block login entirely, use 'suspend' instead.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user revoke\-sessions [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix user revoke\-sessions \-\-id 12
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIstring\fR
Acting admin email (required; unused in this REST\-only CLI \-\- kept for flag compatibility)
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Target user ID (required)
.SS keyorix user suspend
Suspend a user (blocks login)
.PP
Suspend a user account. A suspended user is refused login entirely until reactivated.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user suspend [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
keyorix user suspend \-\-id 12
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fIstring\fR
Acting admin email (required; unused in this REST\-only CLI \-\- kept for flag compatibility)
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIuint\fR
Target user ID (required)
.SS keyorix user suspend\-inactive
Suspend users who have been inactive beyond a threshold
.PP
Suspend all non\-admin users whose last login (or account creation, if they have never logged in) is older than \-\-days days. Triggers the server\-side job via POST /api/v1/admin/jobs/suspend\-inactive\-users (requires system.write).
.PP
With \-\-dry\-run the command evaluates all users against the threshold but makes no changes \(em it prints what would be suspended.
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user suspend\-inactive [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.nf
# Preview first
keyorix user suspend\-inactive \-\-days 90 \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.PP
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-days\fR \fIint\fR
Inactivity threshold in days (required, must be > 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview which users would be suspended without making changes
.SS keyorix user update
Update a user
.PP
Usage: \fBkeyorix user update [flags]\fR
.PP
Examples:
